---
title: Command receipts and their durable replies, including crash paths (implemented)
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant UI as Shell / agent tool
  participant RT as Runtime::command
  participant GW as Gateway unit of work
  participant Disp as Dispatcher
  participant RC as reply_consumer (ReceiptReplies)
  participant Files as NativeArtifactFiles
  UI->>RT: framed command for the selected operation
  RT->>GW: admission, authority, receipt lookup
  alt same request key, same fingerprint
    GW-->>RT: Recorded { replayed: true } — the original decision
  else same key, different intent
    GW-->>RT: Rejected IdempotencyConflict (nothing written)
  else new command
    GW->>GW: decide + history + outbox + receipt + reply intent (one transaction)
    GW-->>RT: Recorded { receipt }
    RT->>Disp: wakeup().wake() (best effort, after commit)
  end
  alt lost acknowledgment
    GW-->>RT: CommandStatusUnknown — resolved by history.command_receipt
  end
  RT-->>UI: reply (the UI renders the decision, never a guess)
  Disp->>RC: claim the reply delivery under a fence
  RC->>Files: publish the reply file (staged, flushed, renamed)
  RC->>GW: commit artifact metadata + ReceiptReplyPublished + checkpoint
  Note over Disp,RC: crash after the receipt: next boot requeues the claim and publishes once
  Note over RC,Files: crash after the file, before metadata: artifact recovery removes the orphan generation, the requeued delivery publishes again
  UI->>RT: history.command_receipt(requestKey)
  alt reply not yet published
    RT-->>UI: ViewUnavailable receipt_reply_artifact (retry the same query)
  else held or failed delivery
    RT-->>UI: ViewUnavailable receipt_reply_held (operator resolves the delivery)
  else published
    RT-->>UI: the receipt with its durable typed reply
  end
